ITEM B0 — Hard Blocker: Node-Centred Grid Rebuild & Orography Registration
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Nature of Arrays in orography_grids.npz:
   - The arrays lats (17.5 down to 13.0) and lons (73.5 up to 76.5) generated in compare_orography_grids.py:10–11
     labeled BOX CORNERS of GEE's reduceResolution raster (dem_e5), NOT box centres.
   - GEE transform: [0.25, 0, -180, 0, -0.25, 90] with origin (-180, 90) placed pixel boundaries at integer multiples
     of 0.25°, putting pixel centres at (k+0.5)*0.25° (shifted diagonally by 0.125° or ~19 km from ERA5 nodes).
2. ARCO ERA5 Grid Convention:
   - Point values (nodes) located at exact multiples of 0.25° (L_lat, L_lon).
   - Each node represents the center of an atmospheric cell spanning [L_lat - 0.125, L_lat + 0.125] x [L_lon - 0.125, L_lon + 0.125].
   - Documentation URLs:
     * ECMWF ERA5: https://confluence.ecmwf.int/display/CKB/ERA5%3A+data+documentation#ERA5:datadocumentation-Spatialgrid
     * WeatherBench-2: https://weatherbench2.readthedocs.io/en/latest/data-guide.html
3. CRS Transform for Node-Centred Rebuild:
   - GEE ImageCollection('ECMWF/ERA5/DAILY').first().projection().getInfo():
     {'type': 'Projection', 'crs': 'EPSG:4326', 'transform': [0.25, 0, -180, 0, -0.25, 90]}
   - Node-centred CRS projection constructed:
     ee.Projection('EPSG:4326', [0.25, 0, -180.125, 0, -0.25, 90.125])
   - Under this transform, pixel boundaries are [L - 0.125, L + 0.125] and pixel centres coincide with ERA5 nodes by construction.
4. Village Assignment under Node-Centred Containment:
   - For all 16,943 villages, polygon centroids satisfy |lat_c - node_lat| <= 0.125° and |lon_c - node_lon| <= 0.125°.
   - Count of villages changing assigned node under true node-centred containment vs nearest-node on corner grid: 0 (the nearest node on the quarter-degree lattice is mathematically identical to box containment [L - 0.125, L + 0.125]).
5. Rebuilt 239-Cell Offset Distribution (ERA5 node - SRTM node-box):
   - Valid land cells: 231 / 247 (16 offshore cells without SRTM land).
   - Min: -346.47 m (at 13.50°N, 75.00°E)
   - p1:  -131.98 m
   - p25: -14.72 m
   - p50: +2.86 m
   - Mean: -1.15 m
   - p75: +13.42 m
   - p99: +130.66 m
   - Max: +152.76 m
   (Notice: Mean offset dropped from -15.61 m to -1.15 m, confirming elimination of the 19 km diagonal misregistration).


