ITEM B14 — Implausible-Pairing Audit
------------------------------------
1. Centroid Distance > 0.125° from Assigned Node: 0 villages.
2. Villages where |dz_era5 - dz_srtm_node| > 200 m: 33 villages (all located in steep Ghats escarpment cells where model orography differs from SRTM box mean by > 200 m).
3. Audit of Otavane (code 9474, fine elevation 45.2 m):
   - Centroid: (15.8894°N, 73.8763°E), Sawantwadi taluka, Sindhudurg district, MH.
   - Assigned Node: (16.00°N, 74.00°E) [i=6, j=2].
   - Distance from node: dlat = 0.1106°, dlon = 0.1237° (both <= 0.125°).
   - Node coarse values: ERA5 orography = 484.2 m, SRTM node-box = 535.2 m.
   - dz_era5 = 45.2 - 484.2 = -439.0 m; dz_srtm_node = 45.2 - 535.2 = -490.0 m.
   - Difference |dz_era5 - dz_srtm_node| = 51.0 m.
   - Verdict: Otavane is a genuine coastal lowland village sitting in the south-western corner of an escarpment cell spanning 45 m to 800+ m, correctly contained in its assigned box (not a wrong-box bug).


